.TH DOLPHIN-CONTEXT-ACTIONS 1 "July 2026" "dolphin-context-actions 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dolphin-context-actions \- Media conversion and file-linking actions for Dolphin's context menu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dolphin-context-actions
[\fI\,--smart-menu\/\fR] [\fI\,--batch MODE\/\fR] [\fI\,--format FMT\/\fR]
[\fI\,--configure\/\fR]
[\fI\,--pick-link-source\/\fR] [\fI\,--cancel-link\/\fR]
[\fI\,--drop-hardlink\/\fR | \fI\,--drop-symlink\/\fR | \fI\,--drop-as TYPE\/\fR]
[\fI\,--target-dir DIR\/\fR]
[\fI\,--hardlink-clone\/\fR | \fI\,--symlink-clone\/\fR | \fI\,--smart-copy\/\fR]
[\fI\,--link-properties\/\fR] [\fI\,--enumerate-hardlinks\/\fR]
[\fI\,files...\/\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdolphin-context-actions\fR is the backend for Dolphin (KDE file manager)
service menus and the \fBkio-plugin\fR context-menu plugin. It provides two
independent feature sets: intelligent, context-aware media conversion, and
Link Shell Extension-style hardlink/symlink operations.
.PP
For media conversion, it detects the MIME type of the selected file and
presents only relevant conversion options via kdialog dialogs, then runs
the chosen conversion using ffmpeg with real-time progress tracking.
.PP
For link operations, it is invoked directly by the \fBkio-plugin\fR context
menu (not through a service menu); dropping into a directory you cannot
write to is handled by a separate, root-owned KAuth helper, not by this
command running elevated. See \fBLINK OPERATIONS\fR below.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-smart-menu\fR
Show the interactive smart menu. Detects file type and presents relevant
conversion actions. This is the mode called by the service menu.
.TP
\fB\-\-batch\fR \fI\,MODE\/\fR
Run a batch conversion without interactive menus. Supported modes:
.RS
.TP
\fBaudio\fR
Convert audio files (use \fB\-\-format\fR to specify target).
.TP
\fBvideo\-to\-gif\fR
Convert video files to animated GIF.
.TP
\fBvideo\-to\-mp4\fR
Transcode video to MP4 (H.264+AAC).
.TP
\fBvideo\-to\-webm\fR
Transcode video to WebM (VP9+Opus).
.TP
\fBextract\-audio\fR
Extract audio track from video to MP3.
.TP
\fBimgur\-upload\fR
Upload images/GIFs/videos to Imgur.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI\,FMT\/\fR
Target format for \fB\-\-batch audio\fR. One of: mp3, ogg, flac, wav, m4a,
opus, alac.
.TP
\fB\-\-configure\fR
Open the configuration dialog to set defaults (audio format, GIF preset,
Imgur Client ID).
.TP
\fB\-\-pick-link-source\fR
Store \fBfiles\fR as the link source for a subsequent drop operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-cancel-link\fR
Clear the picked link source without dropping it.
.TP
\fB\-\-drop-hardlink\fR
Create hardlinks of the picked source(s) in \fB\-\-target-dir\fR. Files only.
.TP
\fB\-\-drop-symlink\fR
Create symlinks of the picked source(s) in \fB\-\-target-dir\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-drop-as\fR \fI\,TYPE\/\fR
Drop the picked source as \fBhardlink\fR, \fBsymlink\fR, \fBhardlink\-clone\fR,
\fBsymlink\-clone\fR, or \fBsmart\-copy\fR into \fB\-\-target-dir\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-target-dir\fR \fI\,DIR\/\fR
Destination directory for a drop operation.
.TP
\fB\-\-hardlink-clone\fR
Clone a picked source directory, hardlinking regular files and recreating
the directory/symlink structure. Requires exactly one picked directory;
prompts interactively for the folder to clone into.
.TP
\fB\-\-symlink-clone\fR
Same as \fB\-\-hardlink-clone\fR but symlinks files instead of hardlinking them.
.TP
\fB\-\-smart-copy\fR
Copy a picked file or directory, preserving internal hardlink and symlink
structure (an internal hardlink stays a hardlink in the copy, not two
independent files). Requires exactly one picked source; prompts
interactively for the folder to copy into.
.SS Name collisions
Every drop and clone renames rather than overwriting or failing when the
name is already used in the destination: \fBname \- Hardlink.ext\fR, then
\fBname \- Hardlink (2).ext\fR, using the first number free in that folder.
The suffix follows the operation \(em \fB\- Symlink\fR, \fB\- Hardlink Clone\fR,
\fB\- Symlink Clone\fR, \fB\- Smart Copy\fR. Directories keep their whole name.
.TP
\fB\-\-link-properties\fR
Show reference count, inode, device, and hardlink sibling paths for \fBfiles\fR
(exactly one file).
.TP
\fB\-\-enumerate-hardlinks\fR
List all hardlink siblings of \fBfiles\fR (exactly one file) found under its
parent directory.
.TP
\fBfiles\fR
One or more file paths to process. Supports %F and %f from Dolphin service
menu substitution.
.SH LINK OPERATIONS
The link flags implement a stateful, Windows Link Shell Extension-style
workflow, driven by the \fBkio-plugin\fR context-menu plugin rather than a
\&.desktop service menu: pick a source, then drop it elsewhere.
.PP
Picked sources are stored in
\fI~/.cache/dolphin-link-extension/picked_sources.json\fR and persist between
invocations. A failed drop keeps the source picked so the operation can be
retried; a successful drop (or \fB\-\-cancel-link\fR) clears it.
.PP
Dropping into a directory this command cannot write to does \fBnot\fR retry
with elevated privileges from within this process. The \fBkio-plugin\fR
context-menu plugin instead calls a separate, root-owned KAuth helper
(\fIkio-plugin/linkhelper.cpp\fR) directly for a single hardlink or symlink
drop, prompting for the administrator password via polkit. Hardlink Clone,
Symlink Clone, and Smart Copy are never offered elevated, since they recurse
over an arbitrarily large, user-controlled tree.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.IP 0
All conversions completed successfully.
.IP 1
One or more errors occurred or the operation was cancelled.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/dolphin-context-actions/config.json\fR
User configuration file. Stores default audio format, GIF preset, and
Imgur Client ID.
.TP
\fI~/.cache/dolphin-link-extension/picked_sources.json\fR
Currently picked link source(s), written by \fB\-\-pick-link-source\fR and
read by every drop operation.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/kio/servicemenus/dolphin-context-actions.desktop\fR
Service menu definition for the smart menu.
.TP
\fI~/.local/share/kio/servicemenus/dolphin-audio-converter.desktop\fR
Service menu definition for the dedicated audio submenu.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Show the smart menu for a GIF file:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-smart\-menu funny.gif
.TP
Batch convert audio files to FLAC:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-batch audio \-\-format flac *.wav
.TP
Convert a video to GIF with medium preset:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-batch video\-to\-gif \-\-format medium clip.mp4
.TP
Upload images to Imgur:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-batch imgur\-upload screenshot.png
.TP
Open configuration:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-configure
.TP
Pick a folder as a link source, then drop a symlink to it elsewhere:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-pick\-link\-source ~/Projects/foo
.br
dolphin-context-actions \-\-drop\-symlink \-\-target\-dir ~/Desktop
.TP
Show link properties for a file:
dolphin-context-actions \-\-link\-properties ~/Projects/foo/bar.txt
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
Python 3.10+
.TP
ffmpeg (>= 4.4) with ffprobe
.TP
kdialog (KDE)
.TP
libnotify
